cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use marina-rules, cite the exact rules your result ran under: the line printed by
  `marina-rules version` or `marina_rules.citation()` (`rules: marina-rules@<version> sha256:<digest>`).
  The version is deliberately not repeated in this file; a result is reproducible only with that line.
title: "marina-rules: point-in-time exchange trading rules as data"
abstract: >-
  The exchange trading rules in force on each day, as data with sources: price limits, stamp duty and fees,
  tick sizes, trading sessions and settlement for China A-shares, China futures, Hong Kong and US equities.
  Every record states when the rule took effect and cites the official text it comes from, with a verbatim
  quote and a content hash.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: David
repository-code: "https://github.com/David-Marina/marina-rules"
url: "https://david-marina.github.io/marina-rules/"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/marina-rules/"
license:
  - CC0-1.0
  - MIT
keywords:
  - point-in-time trading rules
  - backtesting
  - China A-shares
  - price limits
  - stamp duty
  - tick size
  - futures
  - Hong Kong equities
  - US equities
